orld Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132841128,imgsize-89656.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by Marco Rubio: 'God has blessed me in many ways but none more important than my wife Jeanette']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132841078.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-marco-rubio-god-has-blessed-me-in-many-ways-but-none-more-important-than-my-wife-jeanette/articleshow/132841078.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-marco-rubio-god-has-blessed-me-in-many-ways-but-none-more-important-than-my-wife-jeanette/articleshow/132841078.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T01:48:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132841087,imgsize-37988.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote by Ludwig Wittgenstein: 'The real question of life after death isn't whether or not it exists...']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132840908.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Philosopher Ludwig Wittgenstein challenged the preoccupation with life after death, suggesting that eternal existence does not address the fundamental questions of life’s meaning. His reflections emerged amidst the chaos of World War One. In contemporary discussions on digital immortality, this crucial insight often gets overshadowed; authentic meaning resides in fully embracing the present and living with intention.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/quote-of-the-day-by-ludwig-wittgenstein-the-real-question-of-life-after-death-isnt-whether-or-not-it-exists-but-and-why-forever-wont-fix-us/articleshow/132840908.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/quote-of-the-day-by-ludwig-wittgenstein-the-real-question-of-life-after-death-isnt-whether-or-not-it-exists-but-and-why-forever-wont-fix-us/articleshow/132840908.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T01:18:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132840908,imgsize-1208869.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by JS Mill: 'I have learned to seek my happiness by limiting my desires...']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132840677.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Victorian philosopher John Stuart Mill believed that true happiness lies in limiting our desires rather than endlessly pursuing them. After facing a mental crisis due to his upbringing, Mill shifted his philosophy, warning that unending desire leads to a hedonic treadmill. Today, our consumer-driven culture reflects this endless chase; by curbing material wishes, we can unlock a wealth of inner fulfillment and deeper contentment.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/quote-of-the-day-by-js-mill-i-have-learned-to-seek-my-happiness-by-limiting-my-desires-rather-than-and-the-19th-century-cure-for-modern-burnout/articleshow/132840677.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/quote-of-the-day-by-js-mill-i-have-learned-to-seek-my-happiness-by-limiting-my-desires-rather-than-and-the-19th-century-cure-for-modern-burnout/articleshow/132840677.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T01:03:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132840677,imgsize-492588.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Man rejects Rs 2 crore offer in India and chooses $160K in the US because...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132840702.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/man-rejects-rs-2-crore-offer-in-india-and-chooses-160k-in-the-us-because-/articleshow/132840702.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/man-rejects-rs-2-crore-offer-in-india-and-chooses-160k-in-the-us-because-/articleshow/132840702.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T00:48:29+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132840780,imgsize-124268.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1974, Spain imported two tons of American red crayfish for aquaculture; 50 years later...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132840067.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Fifty years ago, American red crayfish were introduced to Spain's Guadalquivir River basin, and they have since established a permanent presence. These aggressive invaders have wreaked havoc on local wildlife and disrupted aquatic ecosystems. Yet, local communities have successfully built an economy around their harvesting and processing. This dependence has sparked legal disputes, resulting in a compromise that permits regulated harvesting, balancing ecological health with economic viability.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1974-spain-imported-two-tons-of-american-red-crayfish-for-aquaculture-50-years-later-the-species-cannot-be-removed/articleshow/132840067.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1974-spain-imported-two-tons-of-american-red-crayfish-for-aquaculture-50-years-later-the-species-cannot-be-removed/articleshow/132840067.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T00:33:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132840067,imgsize-703626.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2022, France promised 1 billion trees within a decade; four years later, a court...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132835728.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[France's top court invalidated a tree-planting funding decree due to procedural flaws.  Ministers failed to consult the public on forestry subsidies impacting biodiversity.  This ruling halts financial support for planting one billion trees over ten years.  The government must now create a new legal framework with public input.  Future funding will focus on restoring damaged forests and promoting diverse tree species.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/in-2022-france-promised-1-billion-trees-within-a-decade-four-years-later-a-court-struck-down-the-decree-funding-the-programme/articleshow/132835728.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/in-2022-france-promised-1-billion-trees-within-a-decade-four-years-later-a-court-struck-down-the-decree-funding-the-programme/articleshow/132835728.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-03T23:40:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132835728,imgsize-1913265.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scottish proverb of the day: "The father buys, the son builds, the grandchild sells and his son..."]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132838319.